{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/d/dad637eac86a819992908d8a7a3d6406f7068347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle STQ = 140^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/f/28ffe9eb0e5eea9e205e7c92df1a45650fdd3d86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PTU = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />, what is the measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/0/57097de258a4671f22ff493dd8ce0e9363e6f0cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle RTU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/0/900e6a5aae842ac17103daea567affa4100837b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 30^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 90^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 50^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 40^{\\circ} \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 140^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"444\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, we can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db1bf40a4a8119b9a32be2b01d22c20a12225e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PQR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/d/c0d3cd9cb6e07993e6e26704aebd812f2bec7c1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle STQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertical_angles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vertical angles\">vertical angles</a>. This means that their measures are equal to each other, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/8/0e801207e6f5b85c284f8c3e868e67567413b6d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle PQR = 140^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>From the diagram, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b30efe74917ddae709c06b2d24bcbb172e628422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle PTR = m\\angle PTU + m\\angle RTU$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"259\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553d1f9c7d0c53f9d7f20568d367214e0fe9be35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle RTU + 90^{\\circ} = 140^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"179\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6ed887038bd5a9acf65c798f57a259ce863e022.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle RTU = 140^{\\circ} - 90^{\\circ} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 50^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"276\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7631e00d1deb6ad3d55301906009f15d342e412a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RS$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is a line segment, so they form <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Straight_angle\" title=\"Straight angle\">straight angles</a>. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/4/82447dc5f95207a28ef44cb7bd3ac8312f8cb806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle PTS + m \\angle STQ = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a69c2159b6fe7121041e1031728d6be40a85398a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle PTS + 140^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/638d8a4acb3cecb36e3fb7a52fd7b6b9aac443c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle PTS = 180^{\\circ} - 140^{\\circ} = 40^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"237\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/3/ad30fc56741329bac99bd3743aeb3f0084c2e5a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\angle PTS + m \\angle PTU + m \\angle RTU = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"315\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/8/148d3467931b80f0dbf50e50b57c9464eb8bfcd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle RTU + 40^{\\circ} + 90^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"227\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15e69d54d56f33bcaa3e398741bdbeae74597329.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle RTU + 130^{\\circ} = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/6/ad6e0099ce42a47d44b100266cf74dd147f67214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\angle RTU = 180^{\\circ} - 130^{\\circ} = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 50^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"285\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 6 (page does 